Theorem RL-9: COW compound contraction (diamond -> single compound instruction)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-9 governs COW compound contraction per Annex E §AIMS COW:
      "COW compound contraction: the diamond IsShared -> Branch ->
      (clone+Set | Set) -> Merge SHALL be contracted into a single compound
      instruction."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - The expanded diamond is the RL-7 Dynamic-mode realization: a runtime
      IsShared test branches to in-place mutation (RC == 1) or
      clone-then-mutate (RC > 1), re-joining at a Merge. The contraction
      fuses the four-block diamond into one compound instruction encoding
      the identical runtime selection.
    - Shipped: emit_rc/cow.rs + realize/decide.rs::decide_annotations emit
      the COW annotation; the compound contraction is a structural rewrite
      over the realized diamond.

  Soundness property:
    Forall COW diamond D (IsShared -> Branch -> {in-place | clone+Set} ->
    Merge) and its contracted compound instruction C:

      (P1) Observational equivalence: for every runtime uniqueness state
           (IsShared == false => unique; IsShared == true => shared), D and C
           select the SAME mutation outcome — in-place on the unique branch,
           copy on the shared branch.

      (P2) Value-semantics preservation: each selected outcome independently
           preserves value semantics — in-place on the genuinely-unique
           runtime branch (no other reference) and copy on the shared
           runtime branch (isolation).

    RL-9 is a structural refinement: the contracted compound instruction is
    observably equivalent to the expanded diamond, so the contraction
    preserves the dual-execution parity invariant (the evaluator and LLVM
    backends see the same COW behavior whether the diamond is expanded or
    contracted).

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine via enumeration of
    both runtime uniqueness states + outcome-equivalence + per-outcome
    value-semantics check.

    Part (P1) — diamond <-> compound equivalence:
      The verifier models the diamond's per-runtime-state outcome and the
      compound's outcome, asserting they agree on every runtime uniqueness
      state:
        runtime_unique = true -> both select in-place (StaticUnique)
        runtime_unique = false -> both select copy (StaticShared)
      A divergence between the diamond and the compound fails the proof.

    Part (P2) — per-outcome soundness:
      Each contracted outcome is independently verified
      value-semantics-preserving (in-place sound on the genuinely-unique
      branch; copy sound on the shared branch).

      Coverage gate: 2 runtime uniqueness states, each with outcome
      equivalence + value-semantics soundness.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl9_cow_compound_contraction; runtime-state
        enumeration + outcome-equivalence + per-outcome value-semantics
        check; emits Fail on an outcome divergence or an unsound contracted
        outcome)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-9 via enumeration of both runtime uniqueness states asserting the contracted compound instruction is observably equivalent to the expanded IsShared diamond (in-place on the unique branch, copy on the shared branch) with a per-outcome value-semantics-preservation check, grounded in the shipped emit_rc/cow.rs + realize/decide.rs COW realization
